### TITLE ###
Valid
### INPUT ###
args:
	name str
	name enum ["alice", "bob", "charlie"]
print("Hi", name)
### ARGS ###
alice
### STDOUT ###
Hi alice

### TITLE ###
ErrorsOnInvalid
### INPUT ###
args:
	name str
	name enum ["alice", "bob", "charlie"]
print("Hi", name)
### ARGS ###
david
### STDERR ###
Invalid 'name' value: david (valid values: alice, bob, charlie)

Usage:
  TestCase <name> [OPTIONS]

Script args:
      --name str   Valid values: [alice, bob, charlie]

Global options:
  -h, --help               Print usage string.
  -i, --interactive        Interactively prompt for script args not already provided, then run.
  -d, --debug              Enables debug output. Intended for Rad script developers.
      --color mode         Control output colorization. Valid values: [auto, always, never] (default auto)
  -q, --quiet              Suppresses some output.
      --confirm-shell      Confirm all shell commands before running them.
      --tls-insecure       Skip TLS certificate verification for all HTTP requests.
      --src                Instead of running the target script, just print it out.
      --reply line:value   Answer a prompt when there's no terminal. Repeatable; repeat a line to answer it again.
      --reply-na line      Assert a prompt won't be reached on this run; rad fails cleanly if it is.
### EXIT ###
1

### TITLE ###
ErrorsIfNonStringEnum
### INPUT ###
args:
    name str
    name enum ["alice", 2]
print("Hi", name)
### ARGS ###
david
### STDERR ###
error[RAD10009]: Unexpected '2'
  --> <script>:3:25
  |
2 |     name str
3 |     name enum ["alice", 2]
  |                         ^
4 | print("Hi", name)
  |
   = info: rad docs RAD10009
### EXIT ###
1

### TITLE ###
CanHaveArgNamedEnum
### INPUT ###
args:
	enum str
	enum enum ["alice", "bob", "charlie"]
print("Hi", enum)
### ARGS ###
alice
### STDOUT ###
Hi alice

### TITLE ###
List elements are each checked
### INPUT ###
args:
    envs str[]
    envs enum ["dev", "stg", "prd"]
print(envs)
### ARGS ###
--envs
dev
--envs
nope
### STDERR ###
Invalid 'envs' value: nope (valid values: dev, stg, prd)

Usage:
  TestCase <envs...> [OPTIONS]

Script args:
      --envs strs   Valid values: [dev, stg, prd]

Global options:
  -h, --help               Print usage string.
  -i, --interactive        Interactively prompt for script args not already provided, then run.
  -d, --debug              Enables debug output. Intended for Rad script developers.
      --color mode         Control output colorization. Valid values: [auto, always, never] (default auto)
  -q, --quiet              Suppresses some output.
      --confirm-shell      Confirm all shell commands before running them.
      --tls-insecure       Skip TLS certificate verification for all HTTP requests.
      --src                Instead of running the target script, just print it out.
      --reply line:value   Answer a prompt when there's no terminal. Repeatable; repeat a line to answer it again.
      --reply-na line      Assert a prompt won't be reached on this run; rad fails cleanly if it is.
### EXIT ###
1

### TITLE ###
Valid list elements pass
### INPUT ###
args:
    envs str[]
    envs enum ["dev", "stg", "prd"]
print(envs)
### ARGS ###
--envs
dev
--envs
prd
### STDOUT ###
[ "dev", "prd" ]

### TITLE ###
Enum on a variadic
### INPUT ###
args:
    *envs str
    envs enum ["dev", "stg", "prd"]
print(envs)
### ARGS ###
dev
nope
### STDERR ###
